#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:5
#: a19705dbe73349eda7be22a320d65c22
msgid "CIRCLE Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:7
#: db479ea27f754477ba0bc153f4591c31
msgid "Circle mode is similar to :ref:`LOITER <loiter-mode>`, but doesn't attempt to hold position. This is primarily meant to be used as an initial failsafe mode to allow the vehicle to turn in order to hopefully regain radio control signal and pilot control. See :ref:`failsafe documentation <apms-failsafe-function>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:13
#: 5de9f3a03ecf44388145902b0f1e4906
msgid "Circle mode is deliberately a very conservative mode, and doesn't rely on GPS positioning as it is used when GPS fails. It will do a large circle, The bank angle is set to the ``ROLL_LIMIT_DEG`` divided by 3, to try to ensure the plane remains stable even without GPS velocity data for accelerometer correction. That is why the circle radius is so large."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:19
#: 5e417bfef97f4a7dacc0ab02e9082122
msgid "Circle mode uses throttle and pitch control to maintain altitude at the altitude where it started circling."
msgstr ""
